      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic center of Pest along the Danube earned UNESCO World Heritage status for its 13th‑century Matthias Church and 19th‑century landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budapest",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pest hosts over 40 museums, including the Hungarian National Museum, the Museum of Fine Arts, and the contemporary Palace of Arts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budapest",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pest is home to the world’s second‑largest synagogue, the third‑largest parliament building, and nearly ten Michelin‑starred restaurants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budapest",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In December 2015, Pest was named a UNESCO City of Design, joining a global network of creative capitals.",
